<title>NETHERLANDS: Hoogovens buys Pechiney unit.</title>
<headline>Hoogovens buys Pechiney unit.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERWIJK, Netherlands 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch steel and aluminium group Hoogovens NV said on Tuesday its German subsidiary Hoogovens Aluminium Bausysteme GmbH had agreed to buy France's Pechiney-Batiment's Alfal division.</p>
<p>Alfal is based near Paris and produces aluminium panels for the construction sector. The company is market leader in France and posted 1995 turnover of about 66 million francs, Hoogovens said in a statement.  </p>
<p>&quot;Alfal will strengthen Hoogovens' position in the French market and serve as much as a nucleus for further expansion,&quot; the Dutch group added.</p>
<p>Hoogovens Aluminium Bausysteme has outlets in Germany, Britain and Belgium and is market leader in the area of aluminium roofings.</p>
<p>No financial details of the transaction with Pechiney were disclosed.</p>
